# #189 Piece 2 (disc 508) — local code-driven membership round-trip
library "Coverage Membership".

/*
Two same-type (Condition) LOCAL concepts + a `first:` decision, to prove CODE-DRIVEN
membership (charter §3/§4): a fact's `code is` — not its `defined by` NAME — decides
which local concept it populates, computed the SAME in the CRE and $apply. Because the
two concepts share a resource type, a mis-coded fact (names one, carries the other's
code) routes to the concept whose SET the code is a member of — the compartment-global
behavior that name-gating would hide. Each concept is `code is` + `definition is exists
this` (the canonical existence reduction; no bare scalar).
*/

concept "Skull Fracture":
- type is Condition.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `skull-fracture`.
- definition is exists this.

concept "Tumor Fracture":
- type is Condition.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `tumor-fracture`.
- definition is exists this.

decision "Coverage Determination":
first:
- when "Skull Fracture" then recommend activity "deny.skull".
- when "Tumor Fracture" then recommend activity "deny.tumor".
- otherwise then recommend activity "approve".

activity "deny.skull":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `Excluded: skull or vertebral fracture.`.

activity "deny.tumor":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `Excluded: tumor-related fracture.`.

activity "approve":
- request CPGServiceRequest.
- with `Approve coverage.`.
